  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Measuring chance and summarising data: the probability scale, combined events with tree diagrams, the three averages, and reading frequency and cumulative-frequency diagrams.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 8.1 — Probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Probability runs from \\( 0 \\) (impossible) to \\( 1 \\) (certain). For equally likely outcomes, \\( P(E)=\\dfrac{\\text{number of favourable outcomes}}{\\text{total number of outcomes}} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Single event",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( P(E)=\\dfrac{\\text{favourable}}{\\text{total}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Complement",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( P(\\text{not }E)=1-P(E) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "AND (independent)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( P(A\\cap B)=P(A)\\,P(B) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "OR (exclusive)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( P(A\\cup B)=P(A)+P(B) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A bag holds 3 red and 5 blue counters. One is drawn at random. Find \\( P(\\text{red}) \\).</p><p>There are \\( 3+5=8 \\) equally likely counters, 3 of them red:</p>\\[ P(\\text{red})=\\frac{3}{8}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the mean of \\( 4,\\,8,\\,10,\\,6,\\,2 \\).</p>\\[ \\bar{x}=\\frac{4+8+10+6+2}{5}=\\frac{30}{5}=6. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Histograms (Frequency Density) <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span>",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "For grouped data with <em>unequal</em> class widths, plot <strong>frequency density</strong> on the \\(y\\)-axis, not frequency. \\(\\text{Frequency density}=\\dfrac{\\text{frequency}}{\\text{class width}}\\). Area of each bar equals the frequency for that class.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Frequency density",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\dfrac{\\text{frequency}}{\\text{class width}}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Frequency from bar",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "area = class width × freq. density",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Cumulative freq.",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Running total of frequencies",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "IQR from box plot",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(Q_3-Q_1\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.C — Histogram",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A class interval 20–30 has frequency 15; class width = 10.</p>\\[\\text{Freq. density}=\\frac{15}{10}=1.5.\\]<p>Conversely, a bar of height 2.4 over interval 30–45 (width 15) represents frequency \\(2.4\\times15=36\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Conditional Probability &amp; Tree Diagrams <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span>",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<strong>Without replacement</strong>: after removing one item, the total decreases, so probabilities on the second branch change. <strong>Conditional probability</strong>: \\(P(A\\mid B)=\\dfrac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)}\\). Multiply along branches for \"and\"; add separate branches for \"or\".",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.D — Tree diagram without replacement",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A bag has 5 red and 3 blue balls. Two balls are drawn without replacement. Find \\(P(\\text{both red})\\).</p>\\[P(\\text{both red})=\\frac{5}{8}\\times\\frac{4}{7}=\\frac{20}{56}=\\frac{5}{14}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Using the same bag (5 red, 3 blue), find the probability of drawing exactly one red ball.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(P(\\text{RB})+P(\\text{BR})=\\dfrac{5}{8}\\cdot\\dfrac{3}{7}+\\dfrac{3}{8}\\cdot\\dfrac{5}{7}=\\dfrac{15}{56}+\\dfrac{15}{56}=\\dfrac{30}{56}=\\dfrac{15}{28}\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
